a local fbi agent was just about a year  into the job when he was called into  work on september 11 2001. thank you for  staying with us i'm brian loftis i'm  denise valdez 20 years later that agent  is telling his story to the i-team's  david charns denise and brian fbi  special agent christopher lamanna has  several reasons to remember september  11th what started as the day he was to  bury his father turned into one  investigating who took down the world  trade center  good morning 64 degrees at eight o'clock  it's tuesday september 11. the sky was  crystal blue there wasn't a cloud in the  sky  and it seemed like the most bluest sky  i've ever seen september 11 2001 means a  few things to christopher lamanna it's  very surreal that 20 years have gone by  it's the day he said goodbye to his  father my dad passed away two days  earlier  from battling lung cancer and the day  terrorists struck his hometown  lamanna now a special agent with the fbi  in las vegas then 29 was about a year  into the job with the fbi in new york  city we were scheduled to bury him  on that tuesday 9 11. a regular  september tuesday  turning into a nightmare some of my  relatives had indicated that they heard  a plane had struck the world trade  center at the funeral paul i had noticed  a number of fbi agents  but when we got to the church they were  all gone soon after he too left his  family said goodbye and got to work i  remember getting home changing out of my  suit  putting on you know other clothes that  were a little more comfortable  because i didn't know what i was going  to be doing i've been inside the world  trade center  so it's very personal  to me because i've walked on the streets  around you know where the world trade  center stood  i had memories there as the towers fell  lamanna rushed downtown i had to go down  there because i knew there were people  down there people that i knew including  his co-worker beth near one of the  towers when it collapsed the debris the  darkness that  enveloped them so quickly  she said she could barely breathe she  saw a glint of an nypd officer's shield  and she grabbed his arm and they worked  their way out of  the area  she was covered  from head to toe she escaped and years  later became lamana's wife  now every september 11th is a time to  remember those moments leading to a  lifetime together moments from that day  and moments with those we've lost i  think about my dad every year  on 9 11 there's a time to mourn but that  was a time for service  i know my dad would have felt the same  way  lamanna has a photo of the new york  skyline with the twin towers at his home  here in the vegas area and he tells me  he spent months working 12-hour shifts  investigating the attacks  and the terrorists he's now working here  at the fbi in las vegas after moving  here with beth several years ago
 

